$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (i) A mixture of 2-chloro-3-iodopyridine (1.2 g, 5.0 mmol),
2-hydroxyphenylboronic acid (1.0 g, 7.5 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (56 mg, 0.25
mmol), PPh3 (132 mg, 0.50 mmol), K3PO4 (2.1 g, 10 mmol), MeCN (20 mL),
and H2O (5.0 mL) was stirred at 50 °C for 20 h.14 MeCN was removed in
vacuo, and the mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 50 mL). The
collected organic layer was dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
The crude product was dissolved in a small amount of CH2Cl2 and excess
hexane was added. 2-(2-chloropyridin-3-yl)phenol as a white solid (0.93
g, 90%). This material was used in the subsequent step without further
purification.
