$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Suzuki cross-coupling of 2-bromo-7-tert-butyl-8-methoxyquinoline and
binol-bisboronic acid A mixture of binol-bisboronic acid derivative (2.01
g, 5 mmol), 2-bromo-7-tert-butyl-8-methoxyquinoline (4.41 g, 15 mmol, 3
equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (578 mg, 0.5 mmol, 0.1 equiv), and Ba(OH)2•8 H2O (9.45
g, 30 mmol, 6 equiv), in a degassed mixture of dioxane (50 mL) and water
(16.7 mL) was heated to 120°C for 24 h. The reaction mixture was then
allowed to cool down to room temperature and the dioxane was removed
using rotary evaporator. The residue was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 50
mL), washed with 1 N HCl (50 mL), brine solution (50 mL), dried over
Na2SO4 and the solvent was evaporated in vacuo. The crude product was
purified by column chromatography over silica gel. The title
tetra-methoxy compound as a white solid, which was recrystallized from
CH2Cl2 and hexane (2.78 g, 75% yield). IR (neat): ν = 2958, 1599, 1507,
1413, 1215, 994 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.66 (s, 2H), 8.12 (q, J
= 8.7 Hz, 4H), 8.03 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.60 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.53
(d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.41-7.44 (m, 2H), 7.25-7.32 (m, 4H), 4.49 (s, 6H),
3.26 (s, 6H), 1.56 (s, 18H) ppm. 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 30.9 (6C),
35.5 (2C), 61.5 (2C), 62.9 (2C), 121.8 (2C), 122.4 (2C), 125.3 (2C),
125.9 (2C), 126.1 (4C), 127.1 (2C), 127.4 (2C), 129.0 (2C), 131.0 (2C),
132.4 (2C), 134.2 (2C), 134.6 (2C), 135.9 (2C), 141.7 (2C), 143.5 (2C),
154.5 (2C), 155.2 (2C), 155.6 (2C) ppm. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for
C50H48N2O4Na [M + Na]+, 763.3512; found 763.3513.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design of a New Bimetallic Catalyst for Asymmetric Epoxidation and
Sulfoxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
