$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 4-(4-cyanophenyl)-5-methyl-isoxazole-3-carboxylate 8n. To a
microwave vial was added methyl 4-bromo-5-methyl-isoxazole-3-carboxylate
2 (809 mg, 3.67 mmol), (4-cyanophenyl)boronic acid (551 mg, 3.67 mmol)
K3PO4 (1.61 g, 7.35 mmol) and 1,1'-bis(di-tert-butylphosphino)ferrocene
palladium dichloride (122 mg, 0.184 mmol). Dioxane (7.35 mL) was added to
the reaction mixture and the vial was purged under vacuum and refilled
with N2 three times. The reaction mixture was stirred in a 100 °C heating
block for 16 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature,
whereupon saturated aqueous NaCl solution (10 mL) was added. The reaction
mixture was extracted with MTBE (3 x 10 mL) and the combined organics
were washed with saturated aqueous NaCl solution (10 mL), dried over
Na2SO4 and concentrated. The crude material was purified by flash column
chromatography (SiO2, eluting with 0-100 % CH2Cl2/isohexane). Isoxazole
8n (659 mg, 2.72 mmol, 74 %) as a pale yellow solid, which was taken on
into the next step without any further purification. m.p. 141-143 °C;
vmax (thin film)/cm-1 2227, 1736, 1619, 1465, 1453, 1321, 1230, 1201,
1172, 1025, 1007, 931, 843; δH (400 MHz, CDCl3) 7.74 (2 H, d, J 8.0),
7.45 (2 H, d, J 8.0), 3.91 (3 H, s), 2.48 (3 H, s); δC (100 MHz, CDCl3)
168.9, 160.3, 153.2, 133.6, 132.1, 130.6, 118.4, 116.3, 112.1, 52.8,
11.5; HRMS (ESI+) C13H10N2O3 + ([M]+) requires 242.0691; found 242.0693
(-0.56 ppm).
